  "notes": [
    "All historical figures are annual and in VeriSign\u2019s reporting currency (USD). Statement values reported in the 10-K as (In millions) were converted to full dollars by multiplying by 1,000,000.",
    "EBIT is proxied as Operating income from the GAAP consolidated statement of comprehensive income (single segment).",
    "D&A (da) is proxied using 'Depreciation of property and equipment' from the consolidated statement of cash flows. VeriSign also has amortization within operating costs (e.g., prepaid registry fees), but that amortization is not provided as a separate cash-flow line item; therefore it is not included in the D&A proxy to avoid double counting.",
    "Capex is proxied using 'Purchases of property and equipment' from the consolidated statement of cash flows and reported as an absolute positive value.",
    "NWC definition used for historical and forecast consistency: NWC = (Total current assets - cash and cash equivalents - marketable securities) - (Total current liabilities - current senior notes). Under this definition, NWC is consistently negative due to deferred revenues; sign is retained in the output.",
    "NWC forecast uses the historical average NWC% of sales approach (constant nwc_pct_sales = -0.755) rather than projecting line-item working-capital mechanics.",
    "Effective tax rate (tax_rate) is set to the average of FY2024 and FY2025 effective tax rates derived from 10-K (income tax expense / income before income taxes).",
    "WACC is an assumption consistent with a CAPM-style cost of equity using a risk-free proxy from DGS10 and a beta proxy, and with after-tax cost of debt derived from interest expense and total senior notes. Treat as model input rather than an exact issuer-provided rate.",
    "Terminal value uses Gordon Growth (terminal_method = gordon_growth) with terminal_growth = 0.02; terminal_exit_ebitda_multiple is null by design.",
    "NOL balance is set using the 10-K disclosure of state net operating loss carryforwards included in deferred tax assets ($23.1 million). NOL utilization percent is left null because the filing does not provide a specific utilization rate suitable for a forward DCF tax attribute model.",
    "Comps: EV/NTM Revenue and EV/NTM EBITDA were not captured from a single consistent primary/high-quality dataset during this run; fields are set to null. Peers\u2019 pe_ntm is populated where a forward P/E proxy was available."
